Subject: [PATCH 1/2] sunxi: H616: detect LPDDR4 or LPDDR3 at boot

Anbernic sells the same H700 handhelds with either LPDDR4 or LPDDR3,
which needed a different SPL each. SUNXI_DRAM_H616_LPDDR4_OR_LPDDR3
builds both types' PHY table and timings. LPDDR4 is tried first, at
AXP_DCDC3_VOLT, and counts only if it trains on the full 32-bit bus
and passes the size check; otherwise DCDC3 goes to
DRAM_SUNXI_LPDDR3_VOLT and LPDDR3 is set up as before, with the
DRAM_SUNXI_LPDDR3_* settings. LPDDR4 goes first so that its chips never
see LPDDR3's higher voltage.

While LPDDR4 is only tried, a DRAM timeout fails the try instead of
stopping, and read calibration's waits, unbounded before, give up
after 1s.
